---
/**
 * t51 · Carrier Arrival
 *
 * Every earlier carrier put the tone spend in the wrong place or hung the
 * tail off the body as an appendage. This is the corrected geometry: a plain
 * rounded-rect body, x 2..29 and y 2..24 at radius 6, and a tail that leaves
 * the bottom-left corner on the same x=6 the body's last row starts on, so the
 * left edge is one continuous line from shoulder to point. Nothing is stuck on.
 *
 * The keyline is derived from the silhouette rather than drawn: any filled
 * pixel with an empty neighbour is ink, which makes it exactly one pixel wide
 * everywhere, including all the way around the tail, with no join to see.
 *
 * The bands are contours of distance from the tail tip, so they curve. The one
 * thing they must never do is settle into horizontal slabs, which is what
 * happens the moment the light source is treated as being far away.
 *
 * The face is the exact family 8×8 — `facePathsAt` at `md` with the
 * `compact` smile and a 2-row gap — centred on the body at (16, 14), tail
 * ignored, with 8 rows of air above it and 7 below. Nothing is cleared
 * for it: the calm field is sized from the glyph itself, so no band edge can
 * reach the face, and white on that one tone measures 5.94:1.
 *
 * 11 purple tones, one ink keyline, no gradients, nothing fetched.
 */
import MarkFrame from '../MarkFrame.astro';
import { facePathsAt } from '../../../data/mark';

interface Props { size?: number }
const { size = 128 } = Astro.props;
---

